# Images are NOT blanket-ignored. `*.png` used to sit here, and that is exactly
# how utils/assets/channel_logo.png -- the watermark the image bakes in from the
# working tree -- stayed untracked: a clean clone built an image with no
# watermark and nothing failed. Generated art is now ignored by its directory
# (the same four dirs Dockerfile.overlay already calls dead) instead, so a new
# source asset is tracked by default and forgetting is loud.
agents/utils/assets/characters/
agents/utils/assets/backgrounds/
agents/utils/assets/effects/
agents/utils/assets/sfx/
# Root-level QA debris from frame grabs and page screenshots. Leading slash so
# this cannot reach a source asset in a subdirectory.
/*.png
/*.jpg
firebase-debug.log
.vercel
*.tsbuildinfo
dashboard/.npm-cache/
agents/venv/
agents/tmp/
# Demo frame grabs at the repo root (sandbox demo renders, not source). Needed
# explicitly because images are no longer blanket-ignored.
tmp/
agents/data/
agents/*.pid
youtube_token.json
keys/

# Real-ESRGAN model binaries (downloaded at runtime)
agents/bin/*.bin
agents/bin/*.param

# Blender — rendered scenes and cache
agents/tmp/blender_render/
agents/tmp/blender_cache/
agents/chroma_db/
agents/media/

# Docker
agents/.venv-docker/
docker-data/
.playwright-mcp/
.env*
.env*.local
com.timi.docker.plist

